==German==
===Etymology===
From {{af|de|Elch|Test}}. Coined in 1997 (after a [[w:Mercedes-Benz|Mercedes-Benz]] overturned during the test at 60 [[km/h]], less than 40 [[mph]]), pejoratively implying one rarely or never needs to perform such maneuvers at the speeds used in the test, except in "exotic" countries such as Sweden, where elk sometimes do get onto the roads.
